# shards' changes to the x86_64 configuration alone, merged after shards.config.

# As many CPUs as a machine has vCPUs at its most, 255 (crates/vmm acpi::MAX_VCPUS: an
# 8-bit APIC id for each but the broadcast's, ACPI 6.5 §5.2.12.2; D13), where Firecracker's
# 64 left a guest of more vCPUs the first 64 ("CPU limit of 64 reached. Ignoring further
# CPUs", arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c l. 267-268), and D191 gives a run one vCPU for
# each host CPU. Within the range Kconfig allows without CPUMASK_OFFSTACK, 2 to 512
# (arch/x86/Kconfig, NR_CPUS_RANGE_END, Linux 6.18); APIC ids to 0xFE, xAPIC's, need no
# x2APIC (Intel SDM Vol. 3A §11.6.2.1), which Firecracker's base has on all the same.
# Per-CPU areas are possible CPUs', which are the CPUs the MADT enumerates (topology.c
# l. 239-241), a machine's vCPUs alone; what NR_CPUS adds of its own, by Kconfig's help
# "about 8KB to the kernel image" each, is unmeasured here (owed: the guest's overhead,
# PM M179 and M183, again on the kernel built with it). Held to acpi::MAX_VCPUS by
# crates/vmm's `the_guest_kernel_takes_every_vcpu_a_machine_has`.
CONFIG_NR_CPUS=255
